fix(compose): wire 3 sheets to real endpoints + fix shareToGroups persistence

Audit caught four wiring bugs in the V2 compose flow that would have
silently 404'd or returned empty results:

  1. TagPeopleSheet was calling /api/social/users/search — that endpoint
     does not exist. Switched to direct supabase.from('profiles')
     .select(id, username, full_name, avatar_url) .or(username.ilike,
     full_name.ilike) — the same pattern the existing global search at
     pages/hub/social-media/index.js:5708 already uses. profiles_select
     RLS is USING(true) so authenticated reads work.

  2. LocationPickerSheet was calling /api/venues/search — also doesn't
     exist. Switched to /api/poker/venues with the documented params
     (search=, lat=, lng=, radius=, limit=). Also fixed the response
     parser: that endpoint returns {success, data: [...]}, not
     {venues: [...]}; defensive fallback chain handles future variants.
     Fixed venue picker to map venue.latitude/longitude (the actual
     column names) into store.location.lat/lng — was hard-coded to
     v.lat/v.lng which were undefined, leading to silent location
     metadata loss.

  3. ShareToGroupsSheet was calling /api/social/home-groups — also
     missing. Switched to direct Supabase reads: union of
     commander_home_groups WHERE owner_id = me AND is_active, with
     commander_home_group_follows JOIN commander_home_groups WHERE
     user_id = me AND is_active. Deduped by group id.

  4. compose.js was calling /api/social/home-groups/post in a
     fire-and-forget loop to mirror the post into each picked group —
     that endpoint also doesn't exist. Real "mirror this post into N
     home group streams" needs the future Hetzner Open Claw worker
     (per CLUB-ARENA-OFFICIAL-UPGRADE-INTEGRATION.md). For now, persist
     the picked group IDs onto the post's metadata.share_to_groups
     JSONB so the future worker can pick them up — no data loss.

Verified clean:
  • social_posts RLS: stale "Anyone can view posts" policy is gone;
    new "Audience-aware view" calls fn_can_view_post.
  • fn_can_view_post(uuid, NULL, NULL) returns TRUE — no regression
    for legacy posts that never had audience_mode set.
  • fn_can_view_post(uuid, 'public', NULL) → TRUE
  • fn_can_view_post(uuid, 'only_me', NULL) → FALSE for non-author
  • fn_can_view_post(uuid, 'invalid_mode', NULL) → FALSE (fail-closed)
  • profiles_select RLS USING(true) — TagPeopleSheet works for any
    authenticated viewer.
  • All modified files pass esbuild --loader:.jsx=jsx parse.
  • SharedPostCreator router.push gated on context==='social-media' so
    club-page and other inline composers are unaffected.

The /api/social/home-groups/post mirror is the only deferred piece;
its absence now degrades gracefully (data preserved in metadata,
no 404 on every post).
